# top-instal-generator — Repo Role

## Role in ecosystem

**Document layer.** Downstream renderer. Receives OfferDTO (or direct config), selects template, fills placeholders, produces DOCX/PDF. Upstream: kalk-top produces OfferDTO; mail-ingress workflow triggers kalk-top which then calls generator; RAG may request document generation via adapter.

## What this repo does NOT do

- Calculate HVAC, selection, buffer, pricing (that is kalk-top)
- Poll Gmail or parse mail (that is topinstal-mail-ingress)
- Own knowledge base or retrieval (that is rag-chat-asystent)
- Add business logic for offer decisions (only render what it receives)

## Local rules

- `mode=from-offer-dto` is the canonical integration path from kalk-top
- REST `POST /wp-json/topinstal/v1/offer-documents/generate` is the system boundary
- Do not guess or infer offer fields; consume what OfferDTO provides
- Keep mapping from OfferDTO to placeholders explicit and lossless where possible

## Cross-repo impact check

Before changing OfferDocumentRequestDTO, from-offer-dto mapping, REST contract, or auth: assess impact on kalk-top (producer of OfferDTO) and any callers. Update `docs/ecosystem/TOPINSTAL_ECOSYSTEM_STATE.md` if contracts change (see update protocol). Sync to kalk-top when possible.

## When unsure

- Does this logic belong here? → Check ecosystem constitution. Generator only renders; it does not calculate.
- Will this break kalk-top integration? → Check `docs/ecosystem/TOPINSTAL_ECOSYSTEM_STATE.md` for current OfferDTO shape and from-offer-dto mapping.
- Should I add calculation or parsing? → No. Redirect to kalk-top or mail-ingress.

## Do not assume ownership

Do not add calculation, mail parsing, or offer decision logic. If the task suggests it, redirect to kalk-top.
